            "\\section{Concluding Remarks} \n",
            "Inspired by GPT3's poor performance in following task instructions, \n",
            "\\cha{\n",
            "we study \\emph{reframing} them. \n",
            "We introduce five approaches that \n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "reformulate task instructions to make them easier,\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "while maintaining their human readability. \n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "Manually applying reframing \n",
            "on 12 tasks, \n",
            "we study their benefits \n",
            "compared to using} raw instructions or fine-tuning mid-sized models.  \n",
            "\n",
            "\\changednew{\n",
            "Reframing can be particularly helpful in applications where task definitions are evolving (making it difficult to crowdsource and fine-tune models), where model designers can come up with new reframed prompts, in a matter of minutes. \n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "\\begin{comment}\n",
            "\\paragraph{Towards a sustainable alternative to model training} \n",
            "In the context of fast prototyping using massive LMs, we hypothesize that further development of reframing can lead to pragmatic alternative to fine-tuning. \n",
            "In applications where task definitions can quickly change \\hanna{what do you mean by quickly change?}, model designers can come up with new reframed prompts, in a matter of minutes. \n",
            "\n",
            "\\end{comment}\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\\begin{comment}\n",
            "\\vspace{-.1cm} \\paragraph{Generalization to future models} \n",
            "Would the reframed prompts remain competitive on future LMs? \n",
            "\n",
            "While it is impossible to decidedly respond to this counterfactual question, \n",
            "extrapolating from Fig.\\ref{fig:fig1b} is a likely evidence that the proposed approach will remain superior, at least in the near term. \n",
            "\n",
            "However, on a longer horizon, the gains depend on the progress of LMs. \n",
            "\n",
            "If models have little difficulty in understanding language, there will be little gain in reframing the instructions.\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\\vspace{-.1cm}\\paragraph{Opportunities for improvement}\n",
            "While reframing enables model development in a human-centric manner, it needs to be applied by model designers. \n",
            "Therefore, an algorithmic solution to reframe tasks will likely be a useful progress forward. This will be part of our future work.\n",
            "\n",
            "\\cha{Some knowledge of the domain is required to be able to design these reframed prompts. Nonetheless, we believe that making this observation and operationalizing it is really important and impactful to the NLP community to fully take advantage of the pre-trained language models, especially in real-world applications.}\n",
            "\n",
            "\\cha{There is a broader problem in the way we (community) evaluate models, beyond this work: almost all SOTA models over-rely on dataset-specific assumptions (the \u201cannotation artifacts\u201d literature~\\cite{gururangan2018annotation, mishra2020dqi, mishra2021robust}). This is a fundamental challenge beyond the scope of our work.}\n",
            "\\end{comment}\n",
            "\n",
            " We hope that this study will inspire further investigation of potentially-unconventional approaches to exploit the knowledge harnessed by increasingly large LMs where fine-tuning and its alternatives are prohibitively expensive.\n",
